# Cloudflare *appends* every matching rule rather than letting the most
# specific one win, so `/*` must not set Cache-Control — a rule here plus a
# rule below would emit both, and a comma-joined pair of conflicting max-ages
# resolves to whichever came first. Documents therefore keep the platform
# default (public, max-age=0, must-revalidate), which is what we want anyway.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Astro fingerprints these, so the filename changes whenever the bytes do.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
